249 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 165 0 R
/E (This query calculates the total revenue generated by each completed transaction. It uses the SELECT clause to display the product name and category, alongside the SUM function to compute the total revenue by multiplying the unit price from the produk table \(p\) by the quantity purchased from the penjualan table \(j\). The JOIN clause merges both tables using the shared id_produk key, while the WHERE filter restricts the analysis exclusively to successful orders with a 'Lunas' status. Finally, the GROUP BY statement aggregates the financial data by product name to provide a clear revenue breakdown for each item.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
